# BigQuery credentials for this dbt project.
#
# Copy to .env.bigquery (gitignored), fill in, then:
#     ENV_FILE=.env.bigquery make check-env             TARGET=bigquery_prod
#     ENV_FILE=.env.bigquery make verify-warehouse-smoke TARGET=bigquery_prod
#     ENV_FILE=.env.bigquery make verify-warehouse       TARGET=bigquery_prod
#
# dbt Core does NOT read .env files itself. The make targets load this file via
# scripts/with_env.py. A bare `dbt build` needs these exported, or use:
#     make dbt CMD="build --target bigquery_prod"

# --- Project ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The GCP project ID (not its display name, not the project number).
BIGQUERY_PROJECT=XXX

# Where datasets are created. Must match the location of any dataset that
# already exists, or BigQuery raises a "Not found: Dataset" that is really a
# region mismatch. EU and US are multi-regions; europe-west2 etc. are regions.
BIGQUERY_LOCATION=EU

# --- Authentication --------------------------------------------------------
# TWO OPTIONS.
#
# (a) No key file -- recommended for local testing. Install the gcloud CLI,
#     run `gcloud auth application-default login`, and use the bigquery_local
#     target, which authenticates as you via Application Default Credentials:
#
#         ENV_FILE=.env.bigquery make verify-warehouse TARGET=bigquery_local
#
#     BIGQUERY_KEYFILE is then unused and can stay as-is. Nothing long-lived
#     is created, so there is no secret to leak or rotate.
#
# (b) A service-account key -- needed for CI and anything unattended, which
#     cannot do an interactive login. Used by the bigquery_prod and
#     bigquery_dev targets. Set BIGQUERY_KEYFILE below.
#
# Absolute path to a service-account JSON key file. The file itself must sit
# OUTSIDE this repo -- do not drop it in the project directory where a stray
# `git add -f` could commit it.
#
# The service account needs, on the project:
#   roles/bigquery.dataEditor  - create datasets and tables
#   roles/bigquery.jobUser     - run queries
#
# This project creates four datasets (extract, seeds, snapshots, transform)
# because custom schemas are absolute rather than prefixed
# (macros/generate_schema_name.sql), so dataEditor at project level is simpler
# than granting per dataset.
BIGQUERY_KEYFILE=/absolute/path/outside/this/repo/bigquery-service-account.json

# --- Cost note -------------------------------------------------------------
# BigQuery bills by bytes scanned. This project's demo dataset is a few hundred
# KB, so a full build costs effectively nothing and stays inside the free tier.
